# Bank 6 (runs at 0xA000). Directives: L label, C line comment, B block
# header, D data range, F row width.
#
# The 8192 bytes are 0xFF. This bank IS mapped (the routine that maps 4/5/6
# puts it in 0xA000, p00:423F and its copies), but nobody reads anything from
# it: it is there because the split goes three at a time and the game only
# needed banks 4 and 5.

B 0xA000 EMPTY BANK
B 0xA000 8192 bytes of 0xFF. It is mapped at 0xA000 together with banks 4 and 5,
B 0xA000 but no instruction reads from it.

D 0xA000 0xC000 filler  0xFF filler: the bank's 8192 bytes, without a single exception.
F 0xA000 16
